# Check out every text file with LF endings, on every platform.
#
# Git for Windows (and GitHub's Windows runners) default to core.autocrlf=true,
# which rewrites LF to CRLF on checkout. That breaks things here in three ways:
# shell scripts staged onto Linux boxes gain a \r on every line, tests that compare
# a file's bytes to what the code staged see different bytes, and anything whose
# integrity binds stored bytes would hash differently on a Windows checkout. Every
# file in the index is already LF, so this changes nothing for macOS or Linux.
* text=auto eol=lf
